  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You conjure a pillar of spellfire in a 20-foot-radius, 20-foot-high Cylinder centered on a point within range. The Cylinder is filled with Bright Light, and each creature in it when it appears makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 4d10 Radiant damage on a failure or half as much on a success. A creature also makes this save when it enters the area for the first time on a turn or ends its turn there, no more than once per turn.</p><p>In addition, whenever a creature in the Cylinder casts a spell, it makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failure, the spell dissipates with no effect, and the action, Bonus Action, or Reaction used to cast it is wasted; if the spell was cast with a spell slot, the slot isn’t expended.</p><p>When you cast this spell, you can choose creatures it doesn’t affect.</p><p><strong>Casting as a Circle Spell.</strong> The spell’s range becomes 1 mile, and it no longer requires Concentration. The number of secondary casters sets its area and duration, as shown in the table below. The spell ends early if any caster who took part contributes to another casting of Spellfire Storm as a Circle spell. In addition to the spell’s usual components, you must provide a special component (a blue star sapphire worth 25,000+ GP), which the spell consumes. When the spell is cast, each secondary caster must expend a level 3+ spell slot; otherwise, the spell fails.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Secondary Casters</th><th>Area of Effect</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1–3</td><td>40-foot-radius, 40-foot-high Cylinder</td><td>1 hour</td></tr><tr><td>4–6</td><td>60-foot-radius, 60-foot-high Cylinder</td><td>8 hours</td></tr><tr><td>7+</td><td>100-foot-radius, 100-foot-high Cylinder</td><td>24 hours</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> The damage increases by 1d10 for each spell slot level above 4.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
